Q: Swipe moves to the end point even when finger not released from swipe control while dragging A: <p>You change the anchors on the fly during the ongoing drag with your first LaunchedEffect. I'm not sure why you do that, the code doesn't seem to make any sense.</p>
<p>Instead, move the anchor definition to the AnchoredDraggableState constructor:</p>
<pre><code>val swipeState = remember {
    AnchoredDraggableState(
        initialValue = false,
        anchors = DraggableAnchors {
            false at 0f
            true at endPx
        },
    )
}
</code></pre>
<p>Then you can remove the first LaunchedEffect and everything should work as intended.</p>
<hr />
<p>Btw., if you also want the action to only execute when the gesture is finished (i.e. the pointer has been released), then you need to use <code>swipeState.settledValue</code> instead of <code>swipeState.currentValue</code> in the second LaunchedEffect.</p>
